config DRM_ACCEL_STRELA
	tristate "STRELA CGRA accelerator"
	depends on DRM_ACCEL
	depends on ARCH_ZYNQ || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on MMU
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_SCHED
	help
	  Choose this option to enable support for the STRELA coarse-grained
	  reconfigurable array, as carried on the programmable logic of a
	  Zynq-7000 (PYNQ-Z2).

	  The CGRA has no IOMMU and no scatter/gather, so its buffers are
	  physically contiguous; they are mapped cached and synchronised
	  explicitly through the interface described in
	  include/uapi/strela_drm.h.

	  Loading the module with sim_dev_count=N registers N simulated devices
	  instead of driving hardware, which is how the driver is tested without
	  an FPGA. A simulated job copies each enabled column from its input to
	  its output and computes nothing.

	  If M is selected, the module will be called strela2.
